_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 7496831, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017ou8pKUsFMFN72fiMMW8HJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 7501923, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` was rounding half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own comment said it used banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). The test expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`, which only happens with banker's rounding, so it failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n\nI couldn't open the FIN-212 document because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID. The fix follows the test and the code comment, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nI didn't merge the PR. That needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DSY5d89Gcfy9N9Ka3MZETY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01J1ruZgmjQEN8DqFBLZjxo5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011DVAh6bDWegxWF4LvUfKt1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BToER1QKTvBPv73ufEFscR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-r